    "created_at": "2023-03-13T06:04:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-13T06:04:45Z",
    "body": "IMO, it might be OK to have the processing model be fairly hand-wavey still, but it needs contain at least one \"must\" or \"should\" statement. Whereas right now the processing model is just\r\n\r\n> User agents must implement the processing model of the [dns-prefetch](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#link-type-dns-prefetch) keyword described in Resource Hints.\r\n\r\nwhich doesn't go anywhere anymore.\r\n\r\nSomething like:\r\n\r\n1. ...Extract out the hostname from the href=\"\" attribute...\r\n\r\n2. Perform a DNS prefetch to _hostname_.\r\n\r\nmight suffice, leaving \"perform a DNS prefetch\" undefined, or trying to define it by reference to some RFC maybe.",
